//==
// # Edge-to-face table: types (complexity sweep, chunk E1)
//
// Sections, in order:
//  - Edge-to-face table

//==
// # Edge-to-face table

// The faces whose bounds cite each edge of a BrepModel, in compressed rows: row e is
// Faces[Offsets[e]] up to Faces[Offsets[e + 1]], the faces citing edge e in increasing face order,
// once each, as layer 2's FacesOfEdge lists them. A coedge naming an edge out of range, and a
// bound naming a loop out of range, are in no row. Offsets has one entry per edge plus one, starts
// at 0 and ends at Faces.Count. The stdlib's JaggedArray<BrepFaceIndex> holds the same data, but
// the C# writer emits no member for a library function whose first parameter is an instance of a
// generic type, so the row accessors need a concrete receiver. Removes: FacesOfEdge's scan of
// every face's coedges per edge in layer 4's discretization.
type EdgeFaceTable
    implements IValue
{
    Offsets: Array<Integer>;
    Faces: Array<BrepFaceIndex>;
}
